sentences.text:
It is well settled proposition of law with regard to defamatory statements made in the complaint,
that in order to establish defamation (a) that till the time of charges levelled against the plaintiff are not disproved or not proved, it could not be said that the allegations in the complaint were without any merits; (b) that the allegations in the complaint could not be said to be defamatory; (c) that a suit for damages for defamation can not be initiated as a counter blast and to use it as a lever to tame the defendant;
O.S. No.556/2025 (d) that the defendant/ complainant cannot be put on a defensive by initiation of such suit for damages for defamation; (e) in case of defamation on the basis of registration of a cognizable offence, it could not be said that the person had been defamed unless and until the said complaint is tested before the appropriate forum;
Musthaq Ahmed vs Misba C on 4 December, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/72608965/
7 20.
